          %p
            The
            %em nerve
            is the right adjoint of a pair of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjoint+functors"} adjoint functors
            that exists in many situations. For the general abstract theory behind this see
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/nerve+and+realization"}> nerve and realization
              \.
          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            As soon as any
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+small+category"} locally small category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            comes equipped with a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+object"} cosimplicial object
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi Δ
                    %mi C
                  %mo :
                  %mi Δ
                  %mo →
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\Delta_C : \Delta \to C
          %p
            that we may think of as determining a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometric+realization"} realization
            of the standard
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplex"} simplex
            in
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/object"} object
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/space+and+quantity"} probeable
            by
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplex"} simplices
            in that there is now a way to find the set
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi N
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi A
                  %msub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi n
                  %mo :
                  %mo =
                  %msub
                    %mi Hom
                    %mi C
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi Δ
                    %mi C
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo ,
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  N(A)_n := Hom_C(\Delta_C[n],A)
          %p
            of ways to map the
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplex"} simplex
            into a given object
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
          %p
            These collections of sets evidently organize into a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+set"} simplicial set
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi N
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo :
                  %msup
