          %h4#PropNerveCat Properties
          %p The following lists some characteristic properties of simplicial sets that are nerves of categories.
          .num_prop
            %h6#proposition Proposition
            %p
              A simplicial set is the nerve of a category precisely if it satisfies the
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Segal+condition"} Segal condition
          %p
            See at
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Segal+condition"} Segal condition
            for more on this.
          %p
          #sSetIsNerveOfCategoryIffAllInnerHornsHaveUniqueFillers.num_prop
            %h6 Proposition
            %p
              %br/
              A
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+set"} simplicial set
              is the nerve of a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/small+category"} small category
              precisely if all
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/inner+horn"} *inner* horns
              have
              %em unique
              fillers.
          %p
            (e.g.
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kerodon"} Kerodon
            = succeed ";" do
              %a{:href => "https://kerodon.net/tag/0031"} Prop. 1.2.3.1
            = succeed ".)" do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/inner+fibration"} inner fibration
          %p
          #sSetIsNerveOfGroupoidIffAllHornsHaveUniqueFillers.num_prop
            %h6 Proposition
            %p
              %br/
              A
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+set"} simplicial set
              is the nerve of a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/groupoid"} groupoid
              precisely if
              %em all
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/horns"} horns
              of dimension
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo &gt;
                    %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \gt 1
              have
              %em unique
              fillers.
          %p
            (cf. e.g.
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kerodon"} Kerodon
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "https://kerodon.net/tag/0037"} Prop. 1.2.4.2
          %p
            Here the point as compared to the previous statements is that in particular all the outer horns have fillers for
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                    %mo &gt;
                    %mn 3
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n \gt 3
